  "intro": "Probability measures how likely an event is, as a number from $0$ to $1$. For equally likely outcomes, $P(A)=\\frac{\\text{favorable outcomes}}{\\text{total outcomes}}$. The complement rule: $P(\\text{not }A)=1-P(A)$. The addition rule: $P(A\\text{ or }B)=P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\text{ and }B)$, which simplifies to $P(A)+P(B)$ for mutually exclusive events. For independent events, $P(A\\text{ and }B)=P(A)\\cdot P(B)$.",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 1,
      "prompt": "A fair die is rolled. Find $P(\\text{even})$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Favorable outcomes (even) are $2,4,6$: three of them.",
          "Total equally likely outcomes: $6$.",
          "$P(\\text{even})=\\frac{3}{6}=\\frac{1}{2}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{2}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 2,
      "prompt": "If $P(A)=0.3$, find $P(\\text{not }A)$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Use the complement rule $P(\\text{not }A)=1-P(A)$.",
          "$1-0.3=0.7$."
        ],
        "answer": "$0.7$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "id": 3,
      "prompt": "Two fair coins are flipped. Find $P(\\text{two heads})$.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "The flips are independent, each with $P(H)=\\frac{1}{2}$.",
          "Multiply: $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{4}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 4,
      "prompt": "$P(\\text{rolling a }5)$ on a fair die.",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "One favorable over six: $\\frac{1}{6}$."
        ],
        "answer": "$\\dfrac{1}{6}$"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "id": 5,
      "prompt": "$P(A\\text{ or }B)$ if mutually exclusive, $P(A)=0.2$, $P(B)=0.5$.",
      "solution": {
